ime if needed we're  very actively taught to fight off  discomfort to fight through discomfort  it's a great tool you know for being on  operations for being in combat it's not  such a great tool when you're hurting  afterwards and so many he says are  hurting in silence but they don't have  to  mic Droid Global News Toronto  the Silver Cross mother next this year's  recipient tells me about her son and the  heavy burden she is honored to bear this  Remembrance Day  foreign  [Music]  Remembrance Day the Silver Cross mother  lays a wreath at the cenotaph in Ottawa  this year it was candy gref from Lacombe  Alberta she represents all the mothers  whose children went off on a military  Mission and never came home  her son Master Corporal Byron gref was  the last Canadian Soldier to die in  Afghanistan I met candy Gruff recently  in Alberta she told me about her son and  the honor of wearing the Silver Cross  he wore his Canadian military uniform  with such Pride his mother candy tells  me now it's one of the few tangible ways  she has left to remember her son Byron I  want to  hold my head up high Walk Tall because  that's what Byron would do and that's  what he would want me to do  mom be proud and I am he was her eldest  child good at hockey mischievous and  goal-oriented he was determined and  funny we all missed that laugh  as a teenager Byron signed up for Cadets  though the family had no history of  serving in the military and then Along  Came grade 12 and he said I would like  to join the military but did you think  immediately that might mean he would be  deployed  at some stage did cross my mind it did  and then I just  trusted that the military  would train him and they did they  trained him very well  his first mission to Afghanistan was in  2007. it was a dangerous time oh my  goodness yes  that phone would ring  or I would see the news and I would see  something had had happened  and your stomach just turns  and you think please please  Byron made it home 